# 🌐 Linux Network Diagnostic Tool

## Project Description

This Bash script performs basic network diagnostics on a Linux Mint system.

It checks:

* Hostname
* IP address
* Network interfaces
* Default gateway
* DNS resolution
* Internet connectivity
* Listening ports
* Routing information

## Script

```bash
#!/bin/bash

echo "======================================"
echo "       LINUX NETWORK DIAGNOSTIC"
echo "======================================"

echo ""
echo "HOSTNAME"
echo "--------------------------------------"
hostname

echo ""
echo "NETWORK INTERFACES"
echo "--------------------------------------"
ip addr

echo ""
echo "IP ADDRESS"
echo "--------------------------------------"
hostname -I

echo ""
echo "DEFAULT GATEWAY"
echo "--------------------------------------"
ip route | grep default

echo ""
echo "DNS TEST"
echo "--------------------------------------"

if getent hosts google.com > /dev/null 2>&1; then
    echo "DNS Resolution: WORKING"
else
    echo "DNS Resolution: FAILED"
fi

echo ""
echo "INTERNET CONNECTIVITY"
echo "--------------------------------------"

if ping -c 4 -W 2 google.com > /dev/null 2>&1; then
    echo "Internet Connection: ONLINE"
else
    echo "Internet Connection: OFFLINE"
fi

echo ""
echo "LISTENING PORTS"
echo "--------------------------------------"
ss -tuln

echo ""
echo "ROUTING TABLE"
echo "--------------------------------------"
ip route

echo ""
echo "======================================"
echo "       NETWORK CHECK COMPLETE"
echo "======================================"
```

## How to Run

```bash
chmod +x network-diagnostic.sh
```

Then:

```bash
./network-diagnostic.sh
```

